^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x),$ $a=1,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+16}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{2}}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]-[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-353191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-353191" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-353191" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ for $x\\in [0,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}),$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2x}-2+{e}^{-2x})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2x}+2+{e}^{-2x})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}{({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})-({e}^{0}-{e}^{-0})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-85665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-352924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{8}$ for $x\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-352924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{8},$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{e}^{8x}-2+{e}^{-8x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{8x}+2+{e}^{-8x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x})^{2}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{{e}^{4x}+{e}^{-4x}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{e}^{4x}-{e}^{-4x}}{8})|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{4(1/2)}-{e}^{-4(1/2)}}{8}]-[\\frac{{e}^{4(0)}-{e}^{-4(0)}}{8}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}-1}{8{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-352924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-352924" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-352924" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^{2}-e^{-2}}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ for $x\\in [1,4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $a=1,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)+\\frac{1}{8}(4)^{2}]-[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{1}{8}(1)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{14}{29}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{4}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-5998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4+\\frac{15}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-362543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [3,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-362543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)^{3/2},$ $a=3,$ and $b=6.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x-3)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x-3}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\sqrt{x-3}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x-2}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}\\sqrt{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}(x-2)^{3/2})|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(6-2)^{3/2}]-[\\frac{2}{3}(3-2)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-362543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-362543" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-362543" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\sqrt{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2+\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1-{x}^{2})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+1)"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-82616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-6002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{1+9{e}^{4x}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-6002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{1+9{e}^{4x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=9{e}^{4x}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm 3{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm 3\\int {e}^{2x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2x}+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb1854cfe68d8a0063c94bdec38c733b04d5400809f"} {"question" "q-6002" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c6fd72147da7c67a05adf07e0dbe952abab3359d696850f85384c39670e3b00c"} {"question" "q-6002" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082094/state.json" "file_sha256" "3232fbdc48098d4fbd9f2eb18